  "description": "Fuaran.Compute.Elementary — the scalar pinned mathematics at the bottom of Fuaran.Compute's package graph: exp, ln, log10 and float-exponent pow behind one special-value table, erfc and the normal distribution, density and quantile, each one argument reduction and one polynomial written with + − × ÷ and comparisons alone, in one order, so their answers are byte-identical on .NET, under Fable and in every host that transcribes them; sin, cos, their pair, atan and atan2, each behind its own table, the argument reduced exactly at every finite double; and Rng, a pinned SplitMix64 generator computed in 16-bit limbs, whose every draw is the same sixty-four bits on every host; and Special, the pinned gamma and beta functions, their logarithms, the regularized incomplete gamma and beta functions, the inverse incomplete beta and the polygamma functions, each measured against a fifty-digit reference. No fused multiply-add and no host mathematics call on any host. FSharp.Core only; Fable-clean.",
